th":"Mul","id":2296,"args":{"angle_bracketed":{"args":[{"type":{"primitive":"f32"}}],"constraints":[]}}},"for":{"borrowed_ref":{"lifetime":null,"is_mutable":false,"type":{"primitive":"f32"}}},"items":[14733,14734],"is_negative":false,"is_synthetic":false,"blanket_impl":null}}},"36533":{"id":36533,"crate_id":0,"name":"_mm512_mask_fnmadd_round_pd","span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\..\\..\\stdarch\\crates\\core_arch\\src\\x86\\avx512f.rs","begin":[9455,1],"end":[9466,2]},"visibility":"public","docs":"Multiply packed double-precision (64-bit) floating-point elements in a and b, add the negated intermediate result to packed elements in c, and store the results in dst using writemask k (elements are copied from a when the corresponding mask bit is not set).\\\n\nRounding is done according to the rounding\\[3:0\\] parameter, which can be one of:\\\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEAREST_INT`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : round to nearest and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEG_INF`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : round down and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_POS_INF`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : round up and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_ZERO`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : truncate and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_CUR_DIRECTION`] : use `MXCSR.RC` - see [`_MM_SET_ROUNDING_MODE`]\n\n[Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=_mm512_mask_fnmadd_round_pd&expand=2728)","links":{"`_MM_FROUND_TO_POS_INF`":35316,"`_MM_SET_ROUNDING_MODE`":35056,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEAREST_INT`":35314,"`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`":35320,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEG_INF`":35315,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_ZERO`":35317,"`_MM_FROUND_CUR_DIRECTION`":35318},"attrs":[{"other":"#[<cfg_attr_trace>(test, assert_instr(vfnmadd, ROUNDING = 8))]"},{"other":"#[rustc_legacy_const_generics(4)]"},{"other":"#[attr = Stability {stability: Stability {level: Stable {since: Version(RustcVersion {major: 1,\nminor: 89, patch: 0})}, feature: \"stdarch_x86_avx512\"}}]"},{"target_feature":