rary\\core\\src\\num\\mod.rs","begin":[1667,1],"end":[1667,58]},"visibility":"public","docs":"Parses an integer from an ASCII-byte slice with digits in a given base.\n\nThe characters are expected to be an optional\n `+` \nsign followed by only digits. Leading and trailing non-digit characters (including\nwhitespace) represent an error. Underscores (which are accepted in Rust literals)\nalso represent an error.\n\nDigits are a subset of these characters, depending on `radix`:\n* `0-9`\n* `a-z`\n* `A-Z`\n\n# Panics\n\nThis function panics if `radix` is not in the range from 2 to 36.\n\n# Examples\n\n```\n#![feature(int_from_ascii)]\n\nassert_eq!(u128::from_ascii_radix(b\"A\", 16), Ok(10));\n```\nTrailing space returns error:\n```\n# #![feature(int_from_ascii)]\n#\nassert!(u128::from_ascii_radix(b\"1 \", 10).is_err());\n```","links":{},"attrs":[{"other":"#[attr = Stability {stability: Stability {level: Unstable {reason: None,\nissue: 134821, is_soft: false}, feature: \"int_from_ascii\"}}]"},{"other":"#[attr = Inline(Hint)]"}],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"function":{"sig":{"inputs":[["src",{"borrowed_ref":{"lifetime":null,"is_mutable":false,"type":{"slice":{"primitive":"u8"}}}}],["radix",{"primitive":"u32"}]],"output":{"resolved_path":{"path":"Result","id":85,"args":{"angle_bracketed":{"args":[{"type":{"primitive":"u128"}},{"type":{"resolved_path":{"path":"ParseIntError","id":733,"args":null}}}],"constraints":[]}}}},"is_c_variadic":false},"generics":{"params":[],"where_predicates":[]},"header":{"is_const":true,"is_unsafe":false,"is_async":false,"abi":"Rust"},"has_body":true}}},"11030":{"id":11030,"crate_id":0,"name":null,"span":{"filename":"library\\core\\src\\convert\\num.rs","begin":[349,1],"end":[349,45]},"visibility":"default","docs":null,"links":{},"attrs":[{"other":"#[attr = ConstStability {stability: PartialConstStability {level: Unstable {reason: None,\nissue: 143773, is_soft: false}, feature: \"const_convert\", promotable: false}}]"},{"other":"#[attr = Stabili