uble-precision (64-bit) floating-point elements in a and b, and subtract the lower element in c from the negated intermediate result. Store the result in the lower element of dst using writemask k (the element is copied from c when mask bit 0 is not set), and copy the upper element from c to the upper element of dst.\\\n\nRounding is done according to the rounding\\[3:0\\] parameter, which can be one of:\\\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEAREST_INT`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : round to nearest and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEG_INF`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : round down and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_POS_INF`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : round up and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_TO_ZERO`] | [`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`] : truncate and suppress exceptions\n* [`_MM_FROUND_CUR_DIRECTION`] : use `MXCSR.RC` - see [`_MM_SET_ROUNDING_MODE`]\n\n[Intel's documentation](https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/docs/intrinsics-guide/index.html#text=mm_mask3_fnmsub_round_sd&expand=2785)","links":{"`_MM_FROUND_TO_POS_INF`":35316,"`_MM_SET_ROUNDING_MODE`":35056,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEAREST_INT`":35314,"`_MM_FROUND_NO_EXC`":35320,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_NEG_INF`":35315,"`_MM_FROUND_TO_ZERO`":35317,"`_MM_FROUND_CUR_DIRECTION`":35318},"attrs":[{"other":"#[<cfg_attr_trace>(test, assert_instr(vfnmsub, ROUNDING = 8))]"},{"other":"#[rustc_legacy_const_generics(4)]"},{"other":"#[attr = Stability {stability: Stability {level: Stable {since: Version(RustcVersion {major: 1,\nminor: 89, patch: 0})}, feature: \"stdarch_x86_avx512\"}}]"},{"target_feature":{"enable":["avx512f"]}},{"other":"#[attr = Inline(Hint)]"}],"deprecation":null,"inner":{"function":{"sig":{"inputs":[["a",{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m128d","id":9314,"args":null}}],["b",{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m128d","id":9314,"args":null}}],["c",{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m128d","id":9314,"args":null}}],["k",{"resolved_path":{"path":"__mmask8","id":35946,"args":null}}],["ROUNDING",{"primitive":"i32"}]],"output":{"resolved_path":{"path":"__m1